OL,3,GNEWSAMore than 50 babies affected by
OL,4,Amaternity closure
OL,5,
OL,6,FMore than 50 babies who should have
OL,7,Fbeen born in north Devon have been
OL,8,Fdelivered in Exeter following the
OL,9,Fsuspension of maternity services at
OL,10,FBarnstaple, a hospital trust has said.
OL,12,FMaternity services at North Devon
OL,13,FDistrict Hospital were temporarily
OL,14,Fsuspended on 11 August with mothers now
OL,15,Fhaving to travel more than an hour to
OL,16,Fthe Royal Devon and Exeter Hospital to
OL,17,Fgive birth.
OL,19,FThe Royal Devon NHS Trust said it had
OL,20,Fensured staff and space were available
OL,21,Fto support women and their families at
OL,22,FExeter hospital.
OL,23,APub: 27-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,345,340,200,160,0,100
